# Materials the preparer writes for a work order, and files the user uploads as capture attachments.
# The ledger rows that point at them live in `data/`, which is ignored — committing the files without
# the rows that give them meaning would put personal work product in version control and still not
# restore to anything usable.
.crossline-materials/
.crossline-attachments/
# Submitted-evidence files (`evidenceAttachmentsRoot`), same reasoning; the e2e suite writes its throwaway ones here too.
.crossline-evidence/

# Written by every `next dev`/`next build`/`tsc` run and different per build directory (`.next`, `.next-e2e`,
# `.next-prod`), so tracking them left the tree dirty after each build. Next's own docs say to ignore
# `next-env.d.ts`; `tsc --noEmit` passes without it.
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# The migration runner's forced pre-migration backup. Named after the database it copied, so it slips
# past the `*.db` patterns above — thirteen of them reached a commit before this line existed.
*.bak
apps/assess/templates/candidates/

# Isolated git worktrees that background agents work in; their work comes back as commits on their own branches.
.claude/worktrees/
